import Principia.FirstEdition.Volume1.Star83Source

namespace PM.RamifiedSyntax

/-!
# Derived propositions of PM I, ✱83

The fifty-four assertions of ✱83 use selections of the membership relation,
domains, images, class products, similarity, and existence/uniqueness claims
built from those constructions.  These are not presently available as
reducible ramified object syntax, while the preceding selection propositions
have no `⊢ᵣ` derivations to cite.  Replacing them by host-language kernels or
opaque atoms would change the asserted formula and violate T3, T6, and T11.

No exact pure theorem can consequently be declared in this module yet.
-/

end PM.RamifiedSyntax
